# Minimal kiosk config for the AI-OS shell (ROADMAP.md Phase 4).
# `webshell_cli` starts a local HTTP server and opens Firefox in --kiosk
# mode against it -- that Firefox window IS the desktop the user sees
# (prompt bar + command/app tile grid), not a terminal. Any other window
# it opens along the way (e.g. `claude auth login`'s own OAuth redirect,
# opened via /usr/local/bin/oais-open-browser -- see build_files/build.sh
# and docs/DECISIONS.md 2026-07-13 for why that wrapper exists instead of
# a bare `firefox`) is fullscreened by the same rule below; webshell/wm.py
# closes it automatically once that login flow's subprocess exits. The
# `/cli` built-in command (webshell/commands.py) spawns `foot` directly --
# also fullscreened.
#
# This kiosk has NO window chrome (no title bar/tab bar/close button) by
# design, so it needs real fallbacks for a human to move between windows
# without relying solely on wm.py guessing right every time:
#   - Alt+Tab / Alt+Shift+Tab: cycle focus between whatever windows are
#     currently open (kiosk shell, a login popup, a /cli terminal) --
#     sway's built-in sibling-cycling, close enough to a real desktop's
#     alt-tab given everything here lives flat in one workspace.
#   - Alt+F4: kill the focused window outright, for anything wm.py's
#     automatic close doesn't catch (swaymsg unavailable, a window it
#     doesn't know to close, etc.).
# Both use Mod1 (Alt) rather than a Super/Mod4 key some keyboards/VMs
# don't forward. Still no bar, no window borders, no other desktop chrome.
#
# stdout/stderr (Python tracebacks, Firefox's own errors -- it's a
# subprocess of webshell_cli, inherits the same fds) are redirected to a
# log file instead of going nowhere: sway takes over the console's
# graphics mode, so anything not captured is simply unrecoverable if this
# fails silently. Switch to another VT (e.g. Ctrl+Alt+F2) and
# `cat ~aios/.local/share/oais/shell.log` (as root, or `sudo -u aios`) to
# read it after a failed boot.

exec sh -c 'mkdir -p "$HOME/.local/share/oais" && cd /usr/lib/oais/orchestrator && exec python3 -m orchestrator.webshell_cli >>"$HOME/.local/share/oais/shell.log" 2>&1'

default_border none
default_floating_border none

bar {
    mode invisible
}

for_window [app_id="firefox"] fullscreen enable
for_window [app_id="foot"] fullscreen enable

bindsym Mod1+Tab focus next
bindsym Mod1+Shift+Tab focus prev
bindsym Mod1+F4 kill
